# .theater-allow — file-level exclusions for theater_scan.py
#
# Copy to the ROOT of the repo being scanned, rename to `.theater-allow`.
#
# PREFER DECLARATION OVER EXCLUSION.
#
# This file excludes whole FILES from scanning. That is a blunt instrument and
# almost always the wrong tool. The right tool is an inline declaration on the
# specific line, which keeps the suppression visible and inventoried:
#
#     - run: pnpm audit --audit-level=high || true   # theater-ok: advisory, tracked RISK-123
#
# A declared suppression PASSES the gate and appears in `--inventory`. An
# excluded file disappears entirely — nobody reviews it again. Use this file
# only for vendored or generated trees you do not own.
#
# SYNTAX
#   path:<regex>    skip a file whose repo-relative path matches
#                   (must start with ^ or contain /)
#
# The scanner rejects broad patterns (`.*`, `.+`, bare fragments under 4 chars)
# and unanchored entries, and that rejection FAILS the run.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Examples, commented out. Uncomment and adapt.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Vendored third-party source we do not maintain.
# path:^vendor/

# Generated client — regenerated on every build, edits do not survive.
# path:^src/generated/

# Fixture tree of deliberately broken samples used by the linter's own tests.
# path:^tests/fixtures/broken/
